// The revl stdlib A2A TASK-LIFECYCLE module (roadmap item 439, issue #118).
//
// `docs/design/439-a2a-task-lifecycle.md` decides that a long-running A2A
// 1.0.0 Task is STREAM-SHAPED, and that its first implementable surface (T1)
// is the four-op explicit-handle projection: a `_start` that returns a handle,
// a `_poll` that reads one lifecycle event, a `_reply` that answers an
// `input-required` / `auth-required` prompt, and a `_cancel`. This module is
// the pure-revl vocabulary those four synthesized crossings speak — the same
// types on BOTH entry points (`through a2a` / `through a2a_rest` on the remote
// row, and `revl import a2a`), so the two projections cannot drift.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------------- purity
// Every declaration here is PURE revl — no `@py`/`@ts` body — so the module
// lowers on every tier and carries no host surface of its own. The taint, the
// crossing, the deadline and the `Faulted`-on-EOF synthesis all live at the
// ADAPTER (the synthesized `@py` body); this module only NAMES the shapes that
// cross. A `TaskEvent` a consumer reads back is `Untrusted[TaskEvent]` because
// the crossing that produced it said so (item 424 D-424c.9), never because of
// anything spelled here.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------- the lifecycle
// A2A 1.0.0 gives a Task the states below. `Unknown` is the adapter's honest
// answer for a state string this binding does not recognise: a peer is a claim
// (item 329), so an unrecognised state is surfaced, never guessed into a
// terminal. `is_terminal` is the single gate a poll loop consults to decide
// whether to stop; it is total over the enum.
//
// A `Faulted` TaskEvent is SYNTHESISED at the adapter (SSE EOF, poll deadline,
// or transport error) — item 130's rule "provider death is a terminal, never
// silence", satisfied at the boundary because the peer cannot be made to
// promise it. It is a `TaskEvent`, not a `TaskState`, because it is the feed's
// terminal, not a state the peer ever reported.
//
// ------------------------------------------------------------ BUMP DISCIPLINE
// Adding, removing or changing a `pub` symbol here bumps
// `stdlib/version.rvl` (see its bump log).

// A handle to a running Task. `id` is the A2A task id; `context` is the
// optional A2A `contextId` that groups related tasks. A `TaskRef` is what a
// `_start` returns and what `_poll` / `_reply` / `_cancel` take back.
pub type TaskRef = { id: Str, context: Opt[Str] }

// The A2A 1.0.0 Task lifecycle states. The first four are non-terminal (the
// task is still live: `input-required` / `auth-required` want a second
// `message/send`); the next four are terminal; `Unknown` is the adapter's
// answer for an unrecognised wire state — surfaced, never coerced.
pub type TaskState = Submitted | Working | InputRequired | AuthRequired
                   | Completed | Failed | Canceled | Rejected | Unknown

// One event read off a Task feed. `Status` reports a lifecycle transition;
// `Artifact` / `Message` carry a text payload the peer produced; `Done`
// carries the terminal payload; `Faulted` is the adapter-synthesised terminal
// for a peer that stopped answering (EOF / deadline / transport error).
pub type TaskEvent = Status(TaskState) | Artifact(Str) | Message(Str)
                   | Done(Str) | Faulted(Str)

// Total: is a lifecycle state one the Task can no longer leave? A poll loop
// stops when this is true. `Unknown` is NOT terminal — a peer that reports a
// state this binding does not recognise may still advance.
pub fn is_terminal(s: TaskState) -> Bool {
  return match s {
    Completed => true,
    Failed => true,
    Canceled => true,
    Rejected => true,
    Submitted => false,
    Working => false,
    InputRequired => false,
    AuthRequired => false,
    Unknown => false,
  }
}

// Total: map an A2A 1.0.0 wire state string to a `TaskState`. An unrecognised
// string is `Unknown` — surfaced, never guessed into a terminal. The adapter
// (the synthesized `@py` body) reads the wire and calls this so the mapping is
// one pure-revl definition shared by every crossing rather than re-derived per
// tier.
pub fn task_state_from_wire(s: Str) -> TaskState {
  if (s == "submitted") { return Submitted }
  if (s == "working") { return Working }
  if (s == "input-required") { return InputRequired }
  if (s == "auth-required") { return AuthRequired }
  if (s == "completed") { return Completed }
  if (s == "failed") { return Failed }
  if (s == "canceled") { return Canceled }
  if (s == "rejected") { return Rejected }
  return Unknown
}
